AUDIO: 'home and powered by the sun. &gt;&gt; We love it because we have this panoramic view all the time. No neighborhood, you can really enjoy the time here, spend really quality time in the city. We live where we drop the'

[00:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'anchor. &gt;&gt; Eric isn\'t just living the dream, he\'s making the dream become reality for his customers, too, building luxury solar-powered catamarans for a booming European market.'

[00:39] [scene:interview]
VISUAL: Arek speaking about the SolarYacht.
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; So, we are producing these boats here in Berlin or close to Berlin and Brandenburg. This one is a trimaran. Some of them are catamaran on the aluminum hull. And aluminum, you just have the to replace them every couple of'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'years. It\'s super easy to deal with aluminum and they are built actually to be on the lake or going from Brandenburg to Amsterdam. We have boats now in Venice and so you can drive it with the regular license for boating. It drives very nice and smoothly straight. Actually, we are now at anchor docked to the solar station charging solar energy and enjoying the &gt;&gt; [music]'

